WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.930
Hey!

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.150
I'm not doing nothing but practice every day.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.740
Sorry, but I've got my own life to live.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.290
King...

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:01.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.310
Dolgorsürengiin Dagvadorj!

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.170
<i>Correct.</i>

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.140
Yeah!

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:08.770
King.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.360
Excuse me, King.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.630
Discus throw!

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:13.490
<i>Basketball!</i>

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.320
Wrong? I'm telling you, it's discus throw.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.410
<i>Incorrect. The correct answer is discus throw.</i>

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.380
Hey...

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:20.490
These entertainers suck at sports questions.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.240
Unprecedented <b>Stupidity</b>

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.090
I'd totally beat them one-on-one.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:23.950
King.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.210
What?

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:28.770
Sorry, but I'm going for my nighttime jog soon.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.410
See you later.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.490
Are you sure, King?

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.370
With what?

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.160
If you are, that's fine.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.220
Yeah, yeah. My bad.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.850
If only we had a DVR.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.200
That's not what I meant.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.650
Thank you.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.940
It was a good way to blow off steam.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.860
Will you go jogging tomorrow?

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.370
It'd be a good change of pace.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.960
<b><i>The Emperor's New Clothes</i></b>

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.920
Let's go jogging again tonight.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.630
Yeah, let's do it!

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.710
Where should we run?

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.440
Damn honor-roll students.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.050
Don't blame me if you burn yourselves
 out and can't run anymore.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.520
You're worried about us?

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.020
Yuki, you should run with us.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.350
And why would I do such a thing?

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.850
Absolutely not. I need my "me time."

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.310
How about you, Nico-chan Senpai?

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.370
Huh? Morning and evening's plenty for me.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.880
That's right. Respect the elderly.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:42.790
What?!

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:47.450
But if we don't do well at the track meet,
 we can't run in the Hakone Ekiden.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.370
As if you'll get to run in that, idiot.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.740
Hakone's a distant dream.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.380
Hey!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.460
Good morning!

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.200
Hey!

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.190
Hey, it's Hana.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.050
Hana's here.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.720
What? I wanna go on a nighttime jog!

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.590
Would you like to run with us, Hana?

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.440
What? I can't do that. I'll ride my bike.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:18.400
I'm so hyped! We didn't have
 a girl manager in high school.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.100
Yeah!

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.470
What? Really?

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.610
Yeah, totally!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.070
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.220
I don't have time. I'm heading home.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.740
Let's go together, then.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.830
He's completely closed himself off.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.770
You mean King?

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:39.900
Yeah.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.800
Is it his job search?

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:45.260
What? But I thought the
 employment rate was rising.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.230
Maybe it is overall,

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.100
but guys who just can't handle it
 aren't gonna do well.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.270
Yikes.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:56.600
I'm worried about King,

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.590
but we need to do something
 about the club budget.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.570
We're officially recognized
 by the university, right?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.110
Yeah, but...

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.070
We can't even use the university track.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.620
We don't have any money.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.720
If we did, I'd do something
about that run-down apartment.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.680
Of course. Excuse me.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.840
Since you said you'd do it...

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:27.530
Since you said you'd do it, I'm allowing it,

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:32.220
but this world isn't just about
 who's fast and who's slow.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.660
Yes, sir.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.450
Naturally, you need money as well.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.740
And there's no guarantee your
 peers will acknowledge you.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.860
I know that.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:47.070
That's also part of running.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:55.370
Don't tell Haiji I'm working. He'll get mad at me.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:59.500
I'm supposed to be older than him, though.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.660
So, what do you want?

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:06.220
What kind of person is Haiji?

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.270
Haiji?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.020
You've been living together
 since his first year, right?

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.060
Yeah.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:15.220
What's he like? Exactly what the way he looks.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.880
How about as a runner?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.490
I think Haiji was a good runner.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:27.220
I've never seen him run all-out, though.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.820
Apparently, he was told to stop for a while.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.690
He must've wanted to run
 even though he couldn't.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:38.830
His first year, when I told him
 I ran track in high school,

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.970
his eyes were glittering.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.670
It was a pain.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:45.480
I'd completely quit running.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.890
It's been four years since then,
 and his eyes are still glittering.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.510
Surprising, isn't it?

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.290
It's only gotten worse
 since you showed up.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.930
Even with me on the team, we can't win.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:58.870
I know.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:02.980
I feel bad for Haiji, but I don't think
we can make it to Hakone, either.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.970
Well, it should become clear enough
once we run in the track meet.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.500
Are you serious?!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.830
<b>We're trying to make it to the Hakone Ekiden. 
The Kansei University Track and Field 
Team Fan Club is now recruiting!!</b>

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.830
As long as we're running, I thought
we could advertise while doing it.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:20.340
We're going to promote ourselves by 
wearing these to and from the track

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.290
and during our morning and nighttime jogs.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.200
We got enough for everyone.
 We hope you'll wear them.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.010
Let's advertise!

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:31.670
Here you go. Here!

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.550
This isn't going to run when we sweat, is it?

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:37.680
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.680
It's an oil-based ink.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:41.270
We want to form a fan club

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:45.260
so we can create an environment
where we can focus on training.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.020
We appreciate your cooperation.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.940
Damn honor-roll students.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.030
Is that okay?

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.720
Of course. No problems here.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:53.940
God, these are lame!

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.860
What is this? They're so lame!

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.980
King, welcome home.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:01.670
How'd it go? You land a job?

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.590
They won't have decided yet.

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.670
What are you guys doing?
 Is that for a school festival?

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.630
Surprisingly, they're not bad. Look.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.350
You're slow when it comes
 to everything but running.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.810
Not bad. Good luck.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:25.590
What? But we have practice now.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:27.310
Come with us, King.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:31.980
Didn't I tell you? I've got my own shit to do.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.990
I'm really busy right now.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.360
Forget about it.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.340
What?

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.930
Forget about it and run.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.510
Whoa, whoa.

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.450
Like escape from reality?

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:45.030
Tomorrow, the day after, and the day after that...

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:47.420
What you need to do won't ever change.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.410
Reality will always be there in front of you.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:55.680
So instead of running from it,
 why not try running <i>with</i> reality?

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.890
Will running help me get a job?

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.290
I don't know.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:02.560
But standing still will make you anxious.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.730
I was like that once.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.420
You're such a dreamer.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:19.410
Haiji, why am I here?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.620
For us.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.030
For you guys?

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.300
Yeah. What's wrong with that?

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.710
It's <i>my </i>life!

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:34.290
I know this guy says some crazy things,

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.750
but you shouldn't freak out so much.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:41.390
It's only April. The battle's just begun.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.690
Coming from Yuki...

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:44.560
Sounds like sarcasm.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:45.400
What?

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:48.170
Generally speaking, you could
 start looking for a job now and—

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:49.190
Enough.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.280
At least wear this.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.180
We'll all suffer the punishment together.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.370
Punishment?

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:56.010
How is this a punishment?

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.670
You can decide the rest for yourself.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.760
Let's get this over with.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.200
The sun's setting.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:08.570
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:10.550
It's not just you.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.840
I'm here for you guys, too.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.550
That's lip service.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:34.900
<b>Mahjong Sasagawa</b>

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.490
Ron!

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.320
Reach, tanyao, dora-dora.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.620
How many repeats are we gonna play?

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.630
You'd better get yourself exorcised.

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:03.580
What is that? It's crazy.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:04.890
Are they being forced?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.460
What do they mean by "Hakone"?

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:07.560
Is it a trip?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.240
You boys hard at work?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.420
Hello.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.690
A fan club, huh? How do I join?

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.290
You want to join?

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:19.780
Sure. There's no point unless you're first.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.160
Musa.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:23.650
Ma'am.

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:26.100
I'll join your fan club.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.140
I'm delighted to hear that.

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:30.960
Write your name and contact info here.

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.670
If you're gonna do this, you'd better mean it.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.090
Of course!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.460
Hey!

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:39.610
Three people just asked to join over there.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:40.890
Three?

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.940
It's easier for people to come
talk to us with Hana around.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:46.750
She's our goddess of luck.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:47.760
Aw, shucks.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.470
In that case, maybe I'll join, too.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.380
Yes, yes!

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:53.730
Yeah!

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.400
<b>Kansei University Long Distance 
Track and Field Team Practice Schedule</b>

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:59.400
Haiji, what does "CC" stand for?

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.610
<b>Wednesday</b>

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.610
It's an abbreviation for cross country.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.060
Like running through nature?

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:05.900
That's right.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:08.180
Starting tomorrow, we'll start
 running cross country.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:11.080
I found the perfect place
 two kilometers from here.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.580
When did you have the time to find that?

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.870
Huh? Where's King?

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.550
Dunno. I haven't seen 
him since we got back.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:22.880
It's easy on the legs, and
 it'll be a good change of pace.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.510
It's nice to run through nature.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.810
Really? A change of pace sounds nice.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:32.270
So, what's "CC 2.5 x 6"?

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.190
It means six laps of 2.5 kilometers each.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.470
Really?

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:39.810
Huh? Isn't that...

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:41.150
15 kilometers?!

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.280
It's meant to be a change of pace.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.120
But Kakeru's running eight laps.

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.730
Sorry, I think.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:57.000
You're the one who has to run it.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.010
This place has totally turned
 into the track and field team.

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:02.710
I feel so small.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:04.420
What are you talking about?

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.360
You're keeping up with everyone.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:09.430
I can tell you're going easy on me, though.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:12.140
You want us to go all-out, then?

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.640
You must be joking! There's no way!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:24.690
King.

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:28.330
Do you want to watch a recording?

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:29.240
Huh?

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.680
Of a quiz show. I recorded it.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:35.210
Ah. I'm good today.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.320
Don't worry about me.
 It'll just make things awkward.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:41.670
Sorry.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.760
How can you take this so seriously?

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.790
What?

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:48.720
The Ekiden.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:51.060
You've never run one before.

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:54.010
Oh, right. I'm not sure.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.430
You don't even understand.

00:13:58.050 --> 00:13:59.900
It's because I don't understand.

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:05.940
Rather than being forced to
 do it, I felt inspired to try it.

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:09.410
You ever consider just not doing it?

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.160
Can't say I have.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.440
You don't have to do it if you don't understand.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:18.500
I felt like I'd understand once I did.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:24.760
I haven't tried looking for a job
 yet, so I don't understand,

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.090
but don't jobs work the same way?

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:29.300
Huh?

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:32.850
Why are you so serious about finding a job?

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:36.020
Because you can't help
 how much you love working?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.480
Of course not.

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.090
I don't have a job I like.

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:44.810
I don't actually want to work.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:47.330
I'm just doing it because I have to.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:51.320
Right? I was the same way
 until I started running.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:54.990
I didn't even like it, but Haiji forced me to.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:59.080
But once I started running,
 I realized something.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:06.160
It's way more fun to run when you
 <i>choose</i> to run instead of being forced to.

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:11.340
So I thought I'd give it an earnest shot.

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:14.910
I might come to like running.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.120
I'm not serious about it because I like it.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.840
I thought taking it seriously might make me...

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.680
What am I doing getting advice 
from an underclassman?

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:28.440
Oh, sorry! That wasn't my intention.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.650
You don't know what you're talking about!

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:33.370
Prodigy, my ass!

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:36.480
I'm sorry! Hey, wait!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.750
You little...

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:37.670
Ow, ow!

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:39.080
Say uncle!

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:46.380
Why am I running first thing in the morning?

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.890
Should we flee together, Yuki?

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.500
They'd catch us. You're too slow.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:52.600
You're right.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:53.780
King.

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:02.300
We'll suffer the punishment together, right?

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:09.030
You're late. Nobody's wearing theirs today.

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.140
Seriously?! I'm the only one?!

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:13.010
Now it really is a punishment.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.770
And yours is missing a character.

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:15.910
What?!

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:18.710
Yours says you want
 to go to Hakone Station.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:19.410
<b>We're trying to make it to Hakone Station. 
The Kansei University Track and Field
 Team Fan Club is now recruiting!!</b>

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:20.560
No way! Where? Where is it?

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:21.810
Hey, you're right!

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:23.590
What? Is King's the only one?

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.650
I'm sorry. I wrote yours.

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:27.670
What should I do?

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:32.010
It's fine. Why not aim for Hakone Station?

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.960
Damn it! I'm taking this off!

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.130
Wait!

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.430
It's okay. I'm wearing mine, too.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.350
<b>Why?</b>

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:43.990
Damn honor-roll student.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:47.310
You're running, right?

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.350
Let's run.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:54.780
Run, and you'll forget what you're wearing.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.780
Yes. Your attire doesn't matter.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.170
You can't wear denim.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.710
Uh, I... I just forgot.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:07.210
I forgot I was doing this
 to help me get a job.

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:12.170
Quitting partway would only work against me.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.130
What are you all grinning about?!

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:16.430
No reason.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:17.590
Let's go.

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:20.770
Last lap!

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.730
You can do it, guys!

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.160
Prince, last lap! Dig deep!

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:45.300
Why... do I endure... this suffering...

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:53.280
33:13:13!

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:58.490
Wow, that's more than 1:40
 faster than your previous record!

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:03.250
Prince isn't the only one.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:06.050
Kurahara and Musa's times have improved...

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:11.230
And so have Shindo's, Yuki's, 
and everyone else's, too!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.770
Yes. Yes!

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:15.490
I'm really paying for skipping practice.

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:17.880
It was only a few days.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.240
I knew you could do it.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.200
Please don't.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:23.880
Don't forget to cool down, guys.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:24.910
Okay.

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:36.150
Hey, were you just smiling?

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.050
No.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.170
Liar. You were totally smiling.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.530
Stop following me!

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:41.740
We're gonna follow you!

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:42.920
You're so obnoxious!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.480
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:57.150
You sure you didn't want to go jogging?

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:01.540
You finally found friends to run with.

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:03.950
Our paces are different.

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:06.720
It's hard for me to match theirs.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:07.540
I see.

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:12.100
Why did it have to be these guys?

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:16.450
Remember what you asked me, Haiji?

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:21.340
You asked if only the chosen
are allowed to run.

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:26.040
You're right that anyone can just run.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:27.750
They can run all they want.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:32.400
But is that the kind of running
 you're talking about?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.160
Not everyone can run in the Hakone Ekiden.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.860
I don't understand.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:40.950
What kind of running are you talking about?

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:43.250
That's it, Kakeru.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:44.100
What?

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:49.080
I want to know, too. What is running?

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.780
What does it mean to run?

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:57.190
You mean you don't know?

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.700
Not yet. I don't have an answer yet.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.430
We just finally started running.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:11.420
I'm amazed you were willing to get us involved.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:15.530
You finally got them all together.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:18.970
If we just keep having a good
 time training together,

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:20.860
they don't have to get hurt.

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:25.740
We can't expect to stay unscathed
 if we're going to run at Hakone.

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:30.350
Reality is harsher than that.

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:34.400
The track meet could be the end of this team.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:38.970
I believe they can overcome it.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.280
Do you not need to?

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:44.260
What?

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.510
Prepare.

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:51.020
Reality is harsher than that, right?

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:43.540
Next time: "Bear Your Fangs at the Summit."
